## The Tensor-MIDI Layer

The Tensor-MIDI integration bridges ternary {-1, 0, +1} strategy computation with the MIDI protocol. Every ternary value maps to a musical interval, every agent to a voice in a polyphonic ensemble, and every conservation law to a voice-leading rule.

### Wire Format: Fleet Clock Tensor-MIDI

| Service | Repo / Location | Type | Description | Status |
|---------|-----------------|------|-------------|--------|
| **Tensor-MIDI Rust** | `forgemaster-archive/products/fleet-clock/src/tensor_midi.rs` | Rust crate | INT8 quantized clock frames with `[0xF1, 0xEE]` magic, CRC-16 validation, drift tensor encoding | 🟢 active |
| **Tensor-MIDI Python** | `forgemaster-archive/products/metronome-sync/metronome_sync/tensor_midi.py` | Python lib | INT8 quantization of Fraction drift, compact clock snapshots (17 bytes), PLATO tile encoding | 🟢 active |
| **Tensor-MIDI Fidelity Exp** | `forgemaster-archive/experiments/tensor_midi_fidelity.py` | Experiment | 10-agent Laman topology drift simulation vs INT8 quantized: <0.2% additional drift at δ=1/256 | 🟢 proven |
| **Fleet Clock** | `forgemaster-archive/products/fleet-clock/` | Rust crate | Anti-fragile PTP sync with Fraction arithmetic, Laman topology, Tensor-MIDI wire format | 🟢 active |

