## The Mapping: Ternary → MIDI

| Ternary Concept | MIDI Concept | Mechanism |
|---|---|---|
| Ternary value (-1, 0, +1) | Interval direction (down, hold, up) | Cumulative sum → pitch |
| Strategy vector | Melody | Sequential values → note sequence |
| Ternary weight mask | Voice leading | Inter-agent weights → harmonic intervals |
| Tick | Beat | 1 tick = 1 beat (BPM = tick rate) |
| Density (non-zero fraction) | Rhythmic density | Fraction of ticks with notes |
| Balance (pos/neg ratio) | Melodic contour | Ascending vs. descending tendency |
| Surprise | Dissonance | High surprise = unexpected interval |
| Conservation | Harmonic stability | γ + H ≈ 1.283 - 0.159·log(V) |
| Species | Musical role | Explorer = soloist, Diplomat = accompanist, etc. |
| Trust | Consonance/Dissonance | +1 = parallel motion, -1 = contrary motion, 0 = independent |
| Energy | Dynamics (velocity) | High energy = loud, low energy = soft |

---

## Wire Protocol Reference

### Fleet Clock Tensor-MIDI Frame

```
[0xF1, 0xEE]   magic         2 bytes
msg_type                      1 byte  (1=Beacon,2=Tick,3=DriftReport,
                                        4=CadenceCall,5=Correction,6=Sunset,
                                        7=Inherit,8=Ack,9=Leave)
sender_id                     1 byte
timestamp_quantized           1 byte  (INT8, scale factor configurable)
payload_len                   1 byte
payload                    variable
crc16                         2 bytes  (CRC-16/HQX)
```

**Total overhead:** 8 bytes + payload

### Clock Snapshot (17 bytes)

```
[4B true_time_num] [4B true_time_den]
[1B offset INT8]
[4B drift_rate_num] [4B drift_rate_den]
```

### Drift Tensor (N × 1 byte)

Each drift value quantized to INT8. At δ = 1/256, additional drift penalty < 0.2%.

---

## MIDI Export Pipeline

```
Arena Session Data → MIDI Mapping → MIDI File (Type 1, multitrack)
                                      ├─ Track 0: Tempo, time sig
                                      ├─ Track 1: Explorer notes (ch. 1)
                                      ├─ Track 2: Diplomat notes (ch. 2)
                                      ├─ Track 3: Marksman notes (ch. 3)
                                      ├─ Track 4: Climber notes (ch. 4)
                                      └─ Track 5: Prospector notes (ch. 5)
```

Each agent's track maps: `pitch = base_note + cumulative_sum(ternary_values)`, `velocity = map(energy, 0..1 → 1..127)`.

